RECORD OF PROCEEDINGS FOR THE GOVERNING BODY
OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE
Office of City Clerk
November 24, 2008
The Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne met in regular session on this date at 6:00
p.m. in Council Chambers.  Present were: MAYOR - Jack R. Spiker; COUNCIL MEMBERS -
Mr. Brown, Ms. Broyles, Ms. Case, Mr. Collins, Mr. Laybourn, Mr. Pierson, Dr. Rinne, Mr.
Segrave and Mr. Valdez.  The pledge of allegiance was recited.

Also present: Carol Intlekofer, City Clerk; Barb Dorr, City Treasurer, and Bob Nicholas,
Acting City Attorney.
Consent Agenda. (All agenda items listed with the designation of [CA] are considered to
be routine items by the governing body and will be enacted by one motion.  There will be no
separate discussion on these items unless a member of the governing body so requests and
support by two other members is received.  Any item removed from the Consent Agenda will be
considered in its normal sequence on the agenda.)  Upon request by Mr. Collins, and pursuant to
support received by Mr. Brown and Dr. Rinne, Mayor Spiker announced agenda item #26(a)
would be removed from the Consent Agenda.  Mr. Collins moved to approve remaining Consent
Agenda items, seconded by Mr. Segrave.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” – all members of the
governing body with the exception of Mr. Laybourn voting “no”.
 [CA]
MINUTES FROM REGULAR MEETING OF THE GOVERNING BODY ON
NOVEMBER 10, 2008.  Motion (per Consent Agenda) carried.
 [CA]
MINUTES FROM VOUCHERS MEETING OF THE GOVERNING BODY ON
NOVEMBER 17, 2008.  Motion (per Consent Agenda) carried.
Mr. Segrave moved to approve payment of vouchers as presented, seconded by Mr.
Valdez. Mr. Brown declared a conflict of interest (business interest) due to a voucher payable to
Ameri-Tech HVAC Services, and vacated Council Chambers. Motion carried.  Voting “yes” –
all members of the governing body present in Council Chambers. Following announcement of
the vote, Mr. Brown returned to Council Chambers.
Mr. Collins moved to limit debate for the current meeting to a maximum of 10 minutes
for any member of the governing body to talk on any one motion, seconded by Mr. Segrave.
Mayor Spiker advised the motion was non-debatable.  Motion carried. Voting “yes” – all
members of the governing body with the exception of Mr. Laybourn voting “no”
Mayor Spiker opened a public hearing for the purpose of receiving comments and input
on the proposed sale of surplus city transit vehicles to other Wyoming governmental entities
known as the Tourism Promotion Joint Powers Board (d/b/a Cheyenne Area Convention and
Visitors Bureau) and the Wind River Transportation Authority.  Joe Dougherty, Cheyenne
Transit Director, explained the purpose of declaring 4 transit vehicles as surplus and proposed
transfer of ownership to other governmental entities pursuant to federal program requirements,
and provided information on the distribution of sales funds between the Federal Transit
