CONSIDERATION OF BIDS:
Consideration of Bid #M-5-09 for a contract between the City of Cheyenne, Parks &
Recreation, and Recco, Inc. d/b/a Five-R Co., Cheyenne WY, for the Cheyenne Youth Activity
and Community Center Project (1% Specific Purpose Sales & Use Tax).  Mark Shubert and John
Fafoutakis spoke in opposition to the amount of expense that would be incurred to renovate the
existing building.  Topics discussed included: Age and condition of the building, wise use of
taxpayer’s money; property acquisition, due diligence efforts, and prior work conducted on the
building.  Mayor Spiker provided information on property acquisition for the park; indicated a
state grant application had been submitted to assist with the cost of renovating the building, and
clarified the type of grant being sought is specific to existing structures only.  Todd Feezer,
Assistant Director, Parks and Recreation, stated input at numerous public meetings held to
determine park amenities included requests that the facility include community gathering space,
and provided information on work that had been accomplished, costs, and architect and
structural engineer inspections that had been conducted which resulted in a portion of the
```

