```text
building being demolished. Rudy Apodaca spoke in support of the contract and inclusion of a
youth activity/community center.  Reporting for Finance Committee, Mr. Segrave moved to
accept the bid in the amount of $1.6 million for Phase I, seconded by Mr. Valdez.  Upon inquiry,
Mr. Feezer reviewed funding sources for the park project involving Phase I and Phase II.
Discussion followed on amenities to be provided; funding; use of existing Parks and Recreation
Neighborhood Facility; design elements; facility staffing and operational costs; future
evolvement of the park; specific purpose sales tax use for land acquisition and park development
costs; funding for Phase I and Phase II development; bidding process, including value
engineering, and grant funding opportunities.  Upon inquiry, Ray Fertig, Recco, Inc., reviewed
aspects of the bid submitted and value engineering items, stating renovations for Phase I would
provide a functioning building with a useable interior.  Motion carried. Voting “yes” – all
members of the governing body with the exception of Mr. Laybourn voting “no”.  (#5321)
