OTHER CITY BUSINESS:
John Fafoutakis expressed his concerns with the signal timing rotation for a traffic light
located at Forest Dr. and Pershing; current and future traffic volume at Walterscheid and West
Allison Road; loud music from vehicle sound systems, and irresponsible pet owners who do not
spay and neuter pets.
Ms. Case referenced a letter Mayor Spiker recently sent to Governor Dave Freudenthal
requesting consideration of additional funding for municipalities during the state’s budget
process to assist with ongoing expenses and revenue shortfalls, and questioned the state’s fiscal
responsibilities to help fund cities and towns.  Mayor Spiker provided information on the
purpose of the letter, noted the effect of reduced monies to municipalities due to the food sales
tax exemption, and advised the Wyoming Association of Municipalities had adopted resolutions
at its state convention in support of pursuing additional state funding to make municipalities
“whole” with regard to food sales tax backfill.
There being no further business to come before the governing body, the meeting was
officially adjourned at 9:12 p.m.
Submitted by,
Carol Intlekofer, MMC
City Clerk
This notice is available in alternative, accessible formats upon request.
